WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.170
In 2007, an IPCC report said 55 per cent
of the Netherlands lay below sea level.

2
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.450
It was wrong.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:14.450
26 per cent is below sea level; 55 per
cent is the share at risk of flooding.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.670
Tuvalu, a Pacific atoll nation, has
a mean elevation of just 2 metres.

5
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.270
So which is more vulnerable, and why?

6
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.630
The country with more land below the sea?

7
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.750
Or are both equally at risk?

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.130
In this mission, you'll
pull risk apart into hazard,

9
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.510
exposure and vulnerability.

10
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.930
Then you'll look inside one society,
using British Columbia's 2021 heatwave.

11
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.090
Your mission: decide whether the
Netherlands or Tuvalu is more vulnerable,

12
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.810
and explain why.
